= Conclusion <conclusion>

The sample demonstrates a complete academic document structure with fictional
content. It offers no empirical finding about any real information retrieval
system. The central lesson is to keep layout settings separate from manuscript
content and to label illustrative data clearly.

Users can replace the three chapter files with their own work, update the
metadata in the configuration file, and add only the references they actually
cite. Before submission, they should check their institution's current format,
declaration, accessibility and electronic submission requirements.
